1
00:00:07,313 --> 00:00:11,851
(This program contains indirect advertisements.)

2
00:00:12,308 --> 00:00:13,818
(Kim Mi Ryeong and Edward Kwon, Aunties Kitchen)

3
00:00:13,818 --> 00:00:15,078
(Lee Yeon Bok and Kim Min Seong, Wandering Panda)

4
00:00:15,078 --> 00:00:16,348
(Hong Seok Cheon and Jung Ho Young, Chef Land)

5
00:00:16,348 --> 00:00:17,588
(Kim Ho Yoon and Kim Kwan Hoon, Crazy Flavor Restaurant)

6
00:00:17,588 --> 00:00:18,718
(Kim Hoon and Choi Sang Hyun, Kids Restaurant)

7
00:00:18,718 --> 00:00:20,118
(Lee Sung Hoon and Go Seok Hyun, Lulu Land)

8
00:00:20,288 --> 00:00:21,758
(Among six alliance teams,)

9
00:00:21,758 --> 00:00:24,358
(only 2 teams to sell 100 servings survive.)

10
00:00:24,358 --> 00:00:25,658
It's over.

11
00:00:25,658 --> 00:00:28,458
(Wandering Panda, Lee Yeon Bok and Kim Min Seong)

12
00:00:28,458 --> 00:00:30,898
(1st place in the 1st half)

13
00:00:30,998 --> 00:00:34,298
(All teams have now entered the second half.)

14
00:00:34,298 --> 00:00:36,298
(Where did everyone flock to at the start of the second half?)

15
00:00:36,298 --> 00:00:37,468
(Ordering)

16
00:00:37,468 --> 00:00:41,738
(Kids Restaurant that put their dessert front and center)

17
00:00:41,738 --> 00:00:43,678
(The 1st survival on Round 3)

18
00:00:43,678 --> 00:00:47,818
(Kids Restaurant, Choi Sang Hyun and Kim Hoon)

19
00:00:47,818 --> 00:00:51,118
(Currently, Wandering Panda is...)

20
00:00:51,118 --> 00:00:54,758
(in last place.)

21
00:00:54,758 --> 00:00:58,088
(Wandering Panda is on the verge of elimination.)

22
00:00:58,088 --> 00:01:00,258
(Now there's only one spot left.)

23
00:01:00,498 --> 00:01:04,168
(Which team will be the final survivor of Round 3?)

24
00:01:04,168 --> 00:01:07,838
(Which team will be the final survivor of Round 3?)

25
00:01:08,968 --> 00:01:11,308
- I'll change the menu outside.
- Okay.

26
00:01:11,738 --> 00:01:14,378
(In 5th place, they start the 2nd half.)

27
00:01:14,538 --> 00:01:15,978
I'll start the second menu item.

28
00:01:15,978 --> 00:01:17,648
That's right. The second item.

29
00:01:17,648 --> 00:01:18,708
Yes.

30
00:01:18,978 --> 00:01:21,578
At first glance, a half and half bowl makes you think...

31
00:01:21,578 --> 00:01:24,818
it'll give you two dishes that most people would enjoy.

32
00:01:26,148 --> 00:01:28,058
For the second half,

33
00:01:28,058 --> 00:01:30,258
we prepared cold perilla oil pasta.

34
00:01:31,428 --> 00:01:32,828
(Perilla oil makguksu has gone beyond a trend...)

35
00:01:32,828 --> 00:01:33,858
(and became a staple.)

36
00:01:33,858 --> 00:01:35,228
It's a really simple combination.

37
00:01:35,428 --> 00:01:38,228
Soy sauce, sugar, and fragrant perilla oil.

38
00:01:38,528 --> 00:01:41,498
Then we fried dried shrimp and ground them up.

39
00:01:44,068 --> 00:01:45,738
We added a little extra umami.

40
00:01:47,208 --> 00:01:49,238
- You're portioning it individually?
- Yes.

41
00:01:49,708 --> 00:01:51,578
When an order comes in, we can just serve it as is.

42
00:01:51,978 --> 00:01:53,348
That way, the flavor doesn't change.

43
00:01:53,348 --> 00:01:55,018
(Perilla oil sauce portioned out per serving)

44
00:01:55,378 --> 00:01:59,148
(It's used according to the number of orders.)

45
00:01:59,148 --> 00:02:00,658
Then Seok Cheon said,

46
00:02:00,718 --> 00:02:02,188
"It's not just about good food."

47
00:02:02,188 --> 00:02:03,988
"Don't we want people to leave feeling full?"

48
00:02:03,988 --> 00:02:05,028
He's right.

49
00:02:05,558 --> 00:02:06,828
We definitely need some meat.

50
00:02:07,398 --> 00:02:09,628
Pork jowl has a really nice texture.

51
00:02:09,628 --> 00:02:12,968
There's chewiness to its rich fat.

52
00:02:13,568 --> 00:02:14,768
We should serve it with the pasta.

53
00:02:16,738 --> 00:02:18,838
With seasoned perilla leaves,

54
00:02:18,838 --> 00:02:20,738
won't it make the perfect combination?

55
00:02:20,738 --> 00:02:22,708
(Shanghai perilla oil pasta and pork jowl suyuk plate, 13 dollars)

56
00:02:22,838 --> 00:02:24,978
Sprinkle this on the meat at the end.

57
00:02:25,148 --> 00:02:26,208
All right.

58
00:02:29,048 --> 00:02:30,748
- There it is.
- Something changed up there too.

59
00:02:31,988 --> 00:02:33,618
"Shanghai perilla oil pasta?"

60
00:02:43,728 --> 00:02:46,468
(A customer shows interest in the second-half menu.)

61
00:02:46,468 --> 00:02:48,738
(2 customers show interest in the 2nd-half menu.)

62
00:02:48,738 --> 00:02:50,968
(4 customers show interest in the 2nd-half menu.)

63
00:02:56,578 --> 00:02:57,708
It changed to...

64
00:02:57,708 --> 00:02:59,208
- Shanghai perilla oil pasta.
- When did it change?

65
00:02:59,408 --> 00:03:01,648
No way. At this rate, we'll never get out of here.

66
00:03:02,748 --> 00:03:04,448
Let's get perilla oil pasta.

67
00:03:05,318 --> 00:03:07,358
I want the perilla oil pasta.

68
00:03:08,458 --> 00:03:10,258
Perilla oil pasta looks delicious.

69
00:03:10,628 --> 00:03:12,928
Shanghai perilla oil... There's also meat.

70
00:03:12,928 --> 00:03:13,998
(As more customers show interest, a waiting line starts to form.)

71
00:03:14,298 --> 00:03:15,728
Orders are in.

72
00:03:16,328 --> 00:03:18,298
This is Shanghai perilla oil pasta.

73
00:03:21,738 --> 00:03:23,568
Chef, I'll make five at the same time.

74
00:03:24,168 --> 00:03:26,008
The churros aren't ready...

75
00:03:26,808 --> 00:03:28,678
(Park Min Hyuk exclaims.)

76
00:03:29,008 --> 00:03:31,408
(Served alongside the second-half menu item)

77
00:03:31,508 --> 00:03:34,618
(Churros)

78
00:03:34,718 --> 00:03:37,518
When I think of amusement parks, churros and cotton candy are...

79
00:03:37,518 --> 00:03:39,748
some of my fondest childhood memories.

80
00:03:39,748 --> 00:03:42,318
So my focus is on churros.

81
00:03:42,318 --> 00:03:43,458
(Chef Land's second-half strategy: Free churros)

82
00:03:43,958 --> 00:03:47,428
(But the churro dough is still being prepared.)

83
00:03:48,758 --> 00:03:51,028
Orders are coming in, so we need to serve fast.

84
00:03:51,028 --> 00:03:52,098
- Okay.
- Okay.

85
00:03:52,898 --> 00:03:55,298
I was outside wearing an octopus costume.

86
00:03:55,298 --> 00:03:58,308
I could see all the waiting lines.

87
00:03:58,708 --> 00:04:01,638
While food was being served continuously by other teams,

88
00:04:01,638 --> 00:04:03,908
we were at a standstill...

89
00:04:03,908 --> 00:04:05,048
especially in the beginning.

90
00:04:07,418 --> 00:04:08,418
Is everything okay?

91
00:04:11,848 --> 00:04:13,518
- I'll try to be on time.
- Okay.

92
00:04:14,558 --> 00:04:16,888
The orders are piling up. We need to get them out immediately.

93
00:04:18,328 --> 00:04:20,458
If churros aren't ready, serve cotton candy instead.

94
00:04:21,558 --> 00:04:22,598
What's the problem?

95
00:04:22,598 --> 00:04:24,228
If not, let's just go with cotton candy.

96
00:04:24,228 --> 00:04:25,298
Yes.

97
00:04:25,328 --> 00:04:27,098
- Serve cotton candy instead.
- Is that okay with you?

98
00:04:27,738 --> 00:04:29,368
- I want to serve this.
- Churros?

99
00:04:29,368 --> 00:04:30,368
Yes.

100
00:04:30,368 --> 00:04:31,708
You can do it.

101
00:04:32,738 --> 00:04:34,608
None of the orders have gone out yet.

102
00:04:34,708 --> 00:04:36,138
- We have ten orders.
- Right.

103
00:04:36,178 --> 00:04:37,678
Food should be ready...

104
00:04:37,678 --> 00:04:39,148
so that the customers can take it immediately.

105
00:04:40,248 --> 00:04:42,548
I definitely asked him before we started.

106
00:04:42,548 --> 00:04:44,718
"What about the churro dough?"

107
00:04:45,148 --> 00:04:46,148
(During prep)

108
00:04:46,148 --> 00:04:47,918
When will you make the churro dough?

109
00:04:48,618 --> 00:04:51,988
When we're about to finish, I'll start making the dough.

110
00:04:52,128 --> 00:04:53,558
You have to make it right before?

111
00:04:53,558 --> 00:04:55,558
The base is choux pastry, so it has to be made right before frying.

112
00:04:55,558 --> 00:04:56,598
I see.

113
00:04:57,928 --> 00:04:59,798
That's so strange.

114
00:05:00,398 --> 00:05:01,398
Can't he just coat them...

115
00:05:01,398 --> 00:05:03,098
with sugar and have them ready beforehand?

116
00:05:04,168 --> 00:05:06,708
I was starting to get worried.

117
00:05:07,208 --> 00:05:08,478
Seok Cheon, can you make cotton candy?

118
00:05:10,238 --> 00:05:11,378
Let's serve them both.

119
00:05:18,318 --> 00:05:20,388
We just need churros and cotton candy.

120
00:05:20,388 --> 00:05:21,488
- Six dishes are ready.
- Okay.

121
00:05:22,788 --> 00:05:25,058
(Restarting the cotton candy operation)

122
00:05:25,058 --> 00:05:26,058
Orders must go out..

123
00:05:26,058 --> 00:05:27,058
- as fast as possible.
- Okay.

124
00:05:29,828 --> 00:05:30,898
Cotton candy...

125
00:05:31,898 --> 00:05:34,138
Here you go. Hurry.

126
00:05:35,868 --> 00:05:37,168
I'll call the customers now.

127
00:05:38,168 --> 00:05:40,908
Tell them that it's cotton candy instead of churros.

128
00:05:40,908 --> 00:05:41,938
Okay.

129
00:05:42,278 --> 00:05:44,048
We're serving cotton candy instead of churros.

130
00:05:44,048 --> 00:05:45,178
(Replaced by Seok Cheon's cotton candy)

131
00:05:45,378 --> 00:05:46,808
Enjoy your food. Thank you.

132
00:05:47,548 --> 00:05:48,578
Enjoy your food.

133
00:05:48,578 --> 00:05:50,148
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.

134
00:05:50,548 --> 00:05:52,288
This cotton candy is free. Thank you.

135
00:05:52,288 --> 00:05:53,488
Enjoy your food.

136
00:05:54,418 --> 00:05:56,458
- Let's keep sending out the orders.
- Okay.

137
00:05:57,528 --> 00:06:00,358
(Staring)

138
00:06:00,698 --> 00:06:02,628
Hoon, if it doesn't work, let's go with cotton candy.

139
00:06:02,628 --> 00:06:03,828
I can make it work.

140
00:06:03,828 --> 00:06:05,368
- You can?
- One batch is...

141
00:06:05,798 --> 00:06:07,268
Give it up fast if it doesn't work.

142
00:06:07,838 --> 00:06:09,398
The speed is important right now.

143
00:06:09,398 --> 00:06:10,908
(Putting the dough into the shaping machine)

144
00:06:11,708 --> 00:06:13,338
We believe in you, Chef Song Hoon.

145
00:06:13,538 --> 00:06:15,408
- I promise to make it work.
- You can do it.

146
00:06:16,908 --> 00:06:20,578
(He finally starts piping out the churros.)

147
00:06:21,378 --> 00:06:23,418
Gosh, why is it so runny?

148
00:06:27,558 --> 00:06:29,458
The churro dough needs...

149
00:06:29,918 --> 00:06:32,658
enough time to be mixed,

150
00:06:32,658 --> 00:06:35,728
cool down, and firm up.

151
00:06:35,728 --> 00:06:38,328
As I rushed it into the shaping machine,

152
00:06:38,328 --> 00:06:39,698
it started getting runny.

153
00:06:40,638 --> 00:06:43,638
Since the dough was already sagging when I fried it,

154
00:06:43,638 --> 00:06:45,668
the churros didn't come out in the right shape.

155
00:06:56,278 --> 00:06:57,388
Hoon, are you okay?

156
00:06:58,218 --> 00:06:59,988
I'll just make cotton candy.

157
00:06:59,988 --> 00:07:02,618
Then take Seok Cheon's place.

158
00:07:02,618 --> 00:07:03,618
Okay.

159
00:07:03,618 --> 00:07:05,528
Could you serve it when I make it?

160
00:07:05,528 --> 00:07:06,558
Instead of shaping it?

161
00:07:06,558 --> 00:07:08,098
That one is ready.

162
00:07:09,458 --> 00:07:11,028
I'm sorry. I should've been more helpful.

163
00:07:11,028 --> 00:07:12,798
Don't say that. We can do it.

164
00:07:13,498 --> 00:07:14,798
You did your best.

165
00:07:16,138 --> 00:07:17,938
(Groaning)

166
00:07:19,768 --> 00:07:20,778
It's not too late.

167
00:07:21,008 --> 00:07:22,438
- It's okay.
- It's okay.

168
00:07:23,878 --> 00:07:26,678
The pasta and pork jowl suyuk were...

169
00:07:26,678 --> 00:07:28,178
prepped and ready to go.

170
00:07:28,548 --> 00:07:29,578
So I thought, "We'll be fine."

171
00:07:30,078 --> 00:07:32,048
We have to trust the team.

172
00:07:34,158 --> 00:07:36,618
- Now it's all about speed.
- Let's hurry.

173
00:07:36,618 --> 00:07:37,828
It's all about speed.

174
00:07:38,158 --> 00:07:39,528
- Let's go.
- Yes.

175
00:07:39,828 --> 00:07:41,558
- Cotton candy is ready.
- Okay.

176
00:07:42,058 --> 00:07:43,458
Thank you.

177
00:07:44,298 --> 00:07:47,638
Enjoy your food. We're serving cotton candy instead of churros.

178
00:07:48,298 --> 00:07:49,498
(Remaining servings: 25)

179
00:07:49,498 --> 00:07:50,538
(Remaining servings: 22)

180
00:07:50,538 --> 00:07:52,068
Thank you. Enjoy your food.

181
00:07:52,068 --> 00:07:53,738
(Remaining servings: 17)

182
00:07:54,108 --> 00:07:56,578
I'll serve enough to satisfy Chef Hong.

183
00:07:56,578 --> 00:07:57,678
- Okay.
- I'll serve generously.

184
00:07:57,678 --> 00:07:59,508
Yes, toss it generously.

185
00:07:59,508 --> 00:08:01,578
- Give them plenty.
- It's a double portion.

186
00:08:01,578 --> 00:08:03,248
- Don't skimp.
- Okay.

187
00:08:03,778 --> 00:08:05,018
Call out the order.

188
00:08:05,218 --> 00:08:06,648
- I'll call right away.
- Right away.

189
00:08:06,648 --> 00:08:08,358
- I'll serve it immediately.
- Yes.

190
00:08:09,158 --> 00:08:10,318
Our teamwork is great.

191
00:08:10,758 --> 00:08:12,958
- You're doing well, Chef Land.
- Way to go, Chef Land.

192
00:08:14,428 --> 00:08:16,798
As we got past the halfway point,

193
00:08:16,798 --> 00:08:18,068
the cooking settled into a rhythm.

194
00:08:18,798 --> 00:08:21,038
Without saying much,

195
00:08:21,038 --> 00:08:23,298
we naturally became one team.

196
00:08:24,208 --> 00:08:25,968
Can you hurry up with the cotton candy?

197
00:08:25,968 --> 00:08:27,338
Okay.

198
00:08:27,478 --> 00:08:30,678
Whose idea was it to make cotton candy in the first place?

199
00:08:30,848 --> 00:08:33,178
- Seok Cheon, this is helping us.
- Right.

200
00:08:33,648 --> 00:08:34,718
Here you go.

201
00:08:34,718 --> 00:08:36,618
I served the seasoned perilla leaves, so please take it.

202
00:08:36,618 --> 00:08:37,848
- I'll take it.
- Okay.

203
00:08:38,188 --> 00:08:39,488
This is good.

204
00:08:40,888 --> 00:08:42,558
How many fried tofu rice balls do you add?

205
00:08:43,188 --> 00:08:44,228
Two in each.

206
00:08:44,988 --> 00:08:47,188
We don't have many left to go.

207
00:08:48,558 --> 00:08:51,268
(Global Lunch Box)

208
00:08:51,798 --> 00:08:53,668
We need to make 15 more.

209
00:08:53,668 --> 00:08:55,168
Fifteen? We can do it.

210
00:08:56,168 --> 00:08:57,368
It was less than I expected.

211
00:08:57,608 --> 00:08:58,708
We could sell it all soon.

212
00:09:00,408 --> 00:09:02,608
I thought that we had a chance to win.

213
00:09:03,178 --> 00:09:04,448
- Do you need shrimp?
- Yes.

214
00:09:04,678 --> 00:09:05,748
I'll give it to you now.

215
00:09:07,078 --> 00:09:08,618
- I'll call them now.
- Sure.

216
00:09:08,618 --> 00:09:09,748
You can call them now.

217
00:09:10,648 --> 00:09:11,888
Chef Jun Seong, here you go.

218
00:09:11,888 --> 00:09:12,948
Thank you.

219
00:09:13,488 --> 00:09:15,288
- Did you order one platter?
- Yes.

220
00:09:15,288 --> 00:09:16,718
This is for you.

221
00:09:17,258 --> 00:09:18,958
Order number 3251.

222
00:09:19,588 --> 00:09:21,558
- Enjoy your food.
- Thank you.

223
00:09:21,798 --> 00:09:22,958
Enjoy your food.

224
00:09:23,658 --> 00:09:24,968
Thank you.

225
00:09:25,898 --> 00:09:27,268
Here you go. Enjoy your food.

226
00:09:30,168 --> 00:09:34,038
A plate is added to Aunties Kitchen as a penalty.

227
00:09:34,538 --> 00:09:35,708
Don't worry about it.

228
00:09:36,008 --> 00:09:38,548
We don't have many left to go anyway.

229
00:09:39,148 --> 00:09:40,448
Another plate is added...

230
00:09:41,148 --> 00:09:43,748
to Aunties Kitchen as a penalty.

231
00:09:45,748 --> 00:09:47,818
(Current Ranking)

232
00:09:47,818 --> 00:09:49,518
Aunties Kitchen is getting penalized all of a sudden.

233
00:09:49,518 --> 00:09:51,028
(3rd place, Kim Mi Ryeong and Edward Kwon)

234
00:09:51,028 --> 00:09:52,458
(Penalty drops them down the rankings.)

235
00:09:52,458 --> 00:09:53,928
(Fighting for 2nd place with 3 servings apart)

236
00:09:54,098 --> 00:09:55,598
What are they serving anyway?

237
00:09:56,298 --> 00:09:58,228
- How did they get so many?
- I know.

238
00:09:59,168 --> 00:10:00,998
(Sighing)

239
00:10:01,898 --> 00:10:03,038
I'm really sensitive...

240
00:10:03,398 --> 00:10:06,168
about ratings and reviews.

241
00:10:06,538 --> 00:10:09,338
It was a huge blow to my pride.

242
00:10:10,208 --> 00:10:12,748
This menu item required a lot of work.

243
00:10:13,178 --> 00:10:16,148
(A lunch box made of 5 different dishes)

244
00:10:16,348 --> 00:10:18,888
We plate everything ahead of time...

245
00:10:19,148 --> 00:10:21,958
and push it through like a conveyor-belt system.

246
00:10:22,258 --> 00:10:26,928
I think the temperature of the food may have been...

247
00:10:27,158 --> 00:10:30,098
what people found disappointing.

248
00:10:30,098 --> 00:10:31,328
That's what I imagine.

249
00:10:32,528 --> 00:10:33,898
There was a lot of variety, so I didn't get tired of it,

250
00:10:33,898 --> 00:10:35,298
but everything was cold.

251
00:10:36,338 --> 00:10:38,008
All the food is cold.

252
00:10:38,508 --> 00:10:39,868
It's been sitting out for too long.

253
00:10:40,778 --> 00:10:41,808
(There was a variety, but the food was too cold.)

254
00:10:41,808 --> 00:10:43,978
(As expected, the food is criticized for being cold.)

255
00:10:43,978 --> 00:10:45,708
(The cheese in tortilla was hard.)

256
00:10:50,618 --> 00:10:53,148
First, let's take out everything that's been squashed.

257
00:10:53,148 --> 00:10:54,488
- Take it all out?
- Yes.

258
00:10:55,458 --> 00:10:57,218
I thought we should grill it again...

259
00:10:59,228 --> 00:11:01,598
and remake it as quickly as possible.

260
00:11:02,258 --> 00:11:04,298
- The shrimp is ready.
- Okay, I'll take it.

261
00:11:05,798 --> 00:11:06,868
Okay, it's done.

262
00:11:07,268 --> 00:11:10,298
I'll serve each of your platter.

263
00:11:10,538 --> 00:11:12,368
- Thank you.
- Thank you. Enjoy your food.

264
00:11:12,368 --> 00:11:13,938
Thank you. Enjoy your food.

265
00:11:14,578 --> 00:11:16,108
All of us are 4 or 5 servings apart.

266
00:11:17,308 --> 00:11:18,408
Let's keep going.

267
00:11:19,078 --> 00:11:20,878
Thank you. Enjoy your food.

268
00:11:21,378 --> 00:11:22,518
I want some ice cream.

269
00:11:22,918 --> 00:11:24,788
The yogurt gelato is 13 dollars.

270
00:11:25,118 --> 00:11:26,888
- We need one more.
- One more.

271
00:11:28,758 --> 00:11:30,388
Hello, it's ready.

272
00:11:31,128 --> 00:11:32,258
What's your order number?

273
00:11:32,928 --> 00:11:35,758
We made this lemon yogurt ice cream from scratch, so you'll like it.

274
00:11:35,958 --> 00:11:38,368
We have about 15 servings left.

275
00:11:38,728 --> 00:11:40,598
Since they haven't announced it yet,

276
00:11:40,598 --> 00:11:43,168
- We're still in the running.
- we're in the running.

277
00:11:43,898 --> 00:11:45,138
This is our final push.

278
00:11:45,138 --> 00:11:47,068
- We can do this.
- Stay strong.

279
00:11:47,738 --> 00:11:51,308
(Only 1 team will survive.)

280
00:11:51,678 --> 00:11:53,078
Someone is making an order.

281
00:11:54,178 --> 00:11:55,978
We expect about three more orders to come in.

282
00:11:55,978 --> 00:11:57,078
Okay. It doesn't matter.

283
00:11:58,148 --> 00:11:59,618
(Ordering)

284
00:11:59,888 --> 00:12:03,018
(Bowing)

285
00:12:03,318 --> 00:12:06,288
(A celebratory dance)

286
00:12:07,358 --> 00:12:08,998
The food will be ready right away.

287
00:12:10,458 --> 00:12:12,768
You'll be served free cotton candy.

288
00:12:13,668 --> 00:12:15,568
It's funny how they're luring people in with cotton candy.

289
00:12:16,238 --> 00:12:17,968
Look, they're luring people.

290
00:12:18,268 --> 00:12:20,368
We have four left.

291
00:12:20,938 --> 00:12:22,878
We need to scoop four more ice creams.

292
00:12:24,038 --> 00:12:25,978
We don't have many left now.

293
00:12:26,348 --> 00:12:28,578
- Did we get four more orders?
- We got quite a lot.

294
00:12:28,578 --> 00:12:30,748
It's fresh gelato made today. Please try it.

295
00:12:31,088 --> 00:12:33,218
Sir, your order will be ready immediately.

296
00:12:33,218 --> 00:12:34,288
(Fighting to survive until the very end)

297
00:12:34,288 --> 00:12:37,258
All right. Someone is making an order.

298
00:12:38,188 --> 00:12:39,888
Your order is ready.

299
00:12:40,658 --> 00:12:42,498
We have our second restaurant...

300
00:12:43,098 --> 00:12:45,828
that sold out all servings.

301
00:12:57,308 --> 00:13:01,348
Chef Land survives after selling out every serving.

302
00:13:01,918 --> 00:13:04,018
(Rushing)

303
00:13:04,118 --> 00:13:07,218
(Jung Ho Young, Song Hoon, Hong Seok Cheon, Park Min Hyuk)

304
00:13:07,218 --> 00:13:10,058
(2nd place, Chef Land survives.)

305
00:13:10,118 --> 00:13:12,158
My gosh.

306
00:13:15,158 --> 00:13:16,898
- It's delicious.
- Isn't it?

307
00:13:17,358 --> 00:13:18,798
It's really good with this.

308
00:13:18,798 --> 00:13:20,728
- Really?
- I like the sauce.

309
00:13:21,168 --> 00:13:22,468
I like this aroma.

310
00:13:22,768 --> 00:13:24,038
The perilla oil aroma is incredible.

311
00:13:24,308 --> 00:13:26,868
- Everything goes well together.
- I know.

312
00:13:27,338 --> 00:13:29,138
How can you get this for just 13 dollars?

313
00:13:29,138 --> 00:13:30,478
This is so good.

314
00:13:30,638 --> 00:13:33,748
If I could find something like this for 13 dollars,

315
00:13:33,748 --> 00:13:35,048
- I'd eat it every day.
- Definitely.

316
00:13:35,178 --> 00:13:38,248
(Without getting any penalty)

317
00:13:38,418 --> 00:13:39,788
(Great texture, nutty, and delicious)

318
00:13:39,788 --> 00:13:41,318
(Great portion and great value, it's simply flawless.)

319
00:13:41,318 --> 00:13:43,258
(They earned a high rating.)

320
00:13:43,618 --> 00:13:46,028
(They started the 2nd half in 5th place.)

321
00:13:47,288 --> 00:13:48,658
(The second-half menu quickly moved them up the rankings.)

322
00:13:48,658 --> 00:13:50,998
The perilla oil dish looks delicious.

323
00:13:50,998 --> 00:13:54,838
(Orders kept pouring in from the start of the second half.)

324
00:13:55,138 --> 00:13:59,038
(From 5th place, they made a comeback to 2nd.)

325
00:13:59,138 --> 00:14:00,838
After the churros problem,

326
00:14:01,078 --> 00:14:03,538
I had pretty much given up.

327
00:14:03,808 --> 00:14:07,278
We felt especially bad because we thought...

328
00:14:07,608 --> 00:14:09,448
we could end up...

329
00:14:09,618 --> 00:14:12,188
hurting Team Goal!

330
00:14:12,448 --> 00:14:14,088
But thankfully, we made it through...

331
00:14:14,588 --> 00:14:15,918
in second place.

332
00:14:16,588 --> 00:14:18,958
You have to admit that you made it through...

333
00:14:19,488 --> 00:14:20,688
because of us.

334
00:14:21,758 --> 00:14:24,228
I'm not as intimidated by you guys anymore.

335
00:14:24,798 --> 00:14:26,368
There will be no more mercy.

336
00:14:28,798 --> 00:14:32,168
With two teams having sold out every single serving,

337
00:14:32,408 --> 00:14:35,508
the 100 serving relay team match is over.

338
00:14:35,738 --> 00:14:38,308
I'm so surprised that we survived!

339
00:14:38,308 --> 00:14:40,578
(1st place, Choi Sang Hyun and Kim Hoon)

340
00:14:40,578 --> 00:14:42,848
(2nd place, Jung Ho Young and Hong Seok Cheon)

341
00:14:46,518 --> 00:14:48,058
My goodness.

342
00:14:49,188 --> 00:14:50,218
Yes!

343
00:14:51,588 --> 00:14:54,528
How can I describe this? It's sad and feels empty.

344
00:14:56,298 --> 00:14:58,328
We lost to the team we were supposed to beat.

345
00:14:59,968 --> 00:15:00,968
It's over.

346
00:15:00,968 --> 00:15:02,798
Once again, I narrowly missed it and ranked third place.

347
00:15:03,438 --> 00:15:04,508
It was so close.

348
00:15:06,538 --> 00:15:07,568
Good job.

349
00:15:07,568 --> 00:15:08,638
Good job.

350
00:15:08,938 --> 00:15:10,278
- Good job.
- Good job.

351
00:15:10,278 --> 00:15:11,678
You too.

352
00:15:12,148 --> 00:15:13,178
Yes.

353
00:15:13,648 --> 00:15:14,848
Good job.

354
00:15:16,648 --> 00:15:17,718
Let's clean up.

355
00:15:18,418 --> 00:15:21,188
I felt deflated and sorry.

356
00:15:21,188 --> 00:15:23,858
I had a lot of mixed feelings.

357
00:15:24,988 --> 00:15:27,628
Let's go home and take a good rest.

358
00:15:27,688 --> 00:15:28,758
The hard work is over.

359
00:15:30,528 --> 00:15:32,298
The 100 serving relay team match.

360
00:15:33,198 --> 00:15:35,838
The first team to successfully sell all the dishes...

361
00:15:37,068 --> 00:15:39,508
and survive is Kids Restaurant.

362
00:15:40,368 --> 00:15:41,378
(1st place, Kids Restaurant, Choi Sang Hyun and Kim Hoon)

363
00:15:41,378 --> 00:15:42,538
- Congratulations.
- Thank you.

364
00:15:42,538 --> 00:15:43,638
Nice.

365
00:15:44,278 --> 00:15:46,008
We targeted kids.

366
00:15:46,578 --> 00:15:49,818
They must've made this with kids in mind.

367
00:15:50,018 --> 00:15:52,218
Free cotton candy.

368
00:15:52,548 --> 00:15:53,648
You came here for this, didn't you?

369
00:15:53,788 --> 00:15:55,558
- I'm looking forward to it.
- Me too.

370
00:15:56,758 --> 00:16:00,728
(They place first with the support of kids and parents.)

371
00:16:01,128 --> 00:16:02,128
Congratulations.

372
00:16:02,128 --> 00:16:04,028
The second team to successfully sell all the dishes...

373
00:16:04,298 --> 00:16:06,728
and survive is Chef Land.

374
00:16:06,728 --> 00:16:08,338
(2nd place, Chef Land, Hong Seok Cheon and Jung Ho Young)

375
00:16:08,338 --> 00:16:11,608
(They came from behind in the second half...)

376
00:16:11,608 --> 00:16:13,408
(without receiving a single penalty with Shanghai perilla oil pasta.)

377
00:16:13,408 --> 00:16:14,478
Good job.

378
00:16:14,938 --> 00:16:17,678
Those who failed to sell out are Kim Mi Ryeong,

379
00:16:17,678 --> 00:16:19,108
(Kim Mi Ryeong)

380
00:16:19,308 --> 00:16:20,448
Edward Kwon,

381
00:16:21,078 --> 00:16:22,178
Kim Ho Yoon,

382
00:16:22,818 --> 00:16:23,848
Kim Kwan Hoon,

383
00:16:24,748 --> 00:16:25,788
Go Seok Hyun,

384
00:16:26,588 --> 00:16:27,618
Lee Sung Hoon,

385
00:16:28,488 --> 00:16:29,488
Lee Yeon Bok,

386
00:16:30,358 --> 00:16:31,358
and Kim Min Seong.

387
00:16:32,258 --> 00:16:34,088
- These eight teams...
- What is it?

388
00:16:43,668 --> 00:16:47,168
will be given one last chance to save the business from closing.

389
00:16:51,908 --> 00:16:53,248
Yes!

390
00:16:53,808 --> 00:16:55,018
Please!

391
00:16:57,048 --> 00:16:58,218
They still have one more chance.

392
00:17:00,918 --> 00:17:02,818
"Is there going to be another repechage?"

393
00:17:03,258 --> 00:17:04,528
"I'll go all out."

394
00:17:04,628 --> 00:17:06,258
"I'll win this no matter what."

395
00:17:06,388 --> 00:17:07,628
I was resolute.

396
00:17:07,628 --> 00:17:11,228
I have another chance to survive.

397
00:17:11,568 --> 00:17:13,628
- Please save us.
- Please.

398
00:17:14,098 --> 00:17:16,038
Will be given one last chance.

399
00:17:17,338 --> 00:17:18,768
- Yes!
- What?

400
00:17:19,368 --> 00:17:21,908
- Be happy.
- Let's stop already.

401
00:17:29,548 --> 00:17:31,018
Each team's representative,

402
00:17:31,918 --> 00:17:33,588
please gather in the middle.

403
00:17:37,418 --> 00:17:38,628
The last chance...

404
00:17:40,988 --> 00:17:42,198
to survive.

405
00:17:42,198 --> 00:17:44,768
(The last chance)

406
00:17:45,168 --> 00:17:46,268
A deathmatch.

407
00:17:47,968 --> 00:17:49,138
It's a boss battle.

408
00:17:49,998 --> 00:17:51,038
Boss battle?

409
00:17:51,038 --> 00:17:53,608
(Boss battle)

410
00:17:53,608 --> 00:17:54,678
What?

411
00:17:55,038 --> 00:17:57,238
- What? A boss battle?
- It's a boss battle.

412
00:17:57,378 --> 00:17:58,548
- What's a boss battle?
- We won't be participating.

413
00:17:58,548 --> 00:17:59,648
- A boss battle.
- Now,

414
00:17:59,908 --> 00:18:01,648
the alliance teams are no longer.

415
00:18:03,048 --> 00:18:04,178
My gosh.

416
00:18:06,248 --> 00:18:07,388
Now, you'll go back...

417
00:18:07,718 --> 00:18:10,188
to eight individual restaurants...

418
00:18:10,488 --> 00:18:12,088
and you'll fight each other.

419
00:18:12,158 --> 00:18:14,328
(Completely individual competition)

420
00:18:14,328 --> 00:18:16,998
Two teams will sell in one booth.

421
00:18:16,998 --> 00:18:18,428
(Lulu Land)

422
00:18:18,428 --> 00:18:21,268
Two kiosks will be placed per booth.

423
00:18:21,268 --> 00:18:23,068
(Order here)

424
00:18:23,068 --> 00:18:24,708
The stoves and kitchen utensils...

425
00:18:25,068 --> 00:18:27,208
are to be used upon agreements between the restaurants.

426
00:18:28,438 --> 00:18:33,478
Out of 8 restaurants, only the first 3 teams to sell 30 plates...

427
00:18:33,478 --> 00:18:34,948
will survive.

428
00:18:35,418 --> 00:18:37,478
The boss battle will also add...

429
00:18:38,148 --> 00:18:40,088
penalty plates.

430
00:18:40,088 --> 00:18:42,258
(Penalty plates will be added with customer dissatisfaction.)

431
00:18:42,918 --> 00:18:44,888
The plate to be used for the boss battle is...

432
00:18:48,458 --> 00:18:50,228
what everyone has avoided.

433
00:18:51,998 --> 00:18:53,168
The cauldron-shaped bowl?

434
00:18:53,398 --> 00:18:55,038
It's the cauldron-shaped bowl.

435
00:18:56,538 --> 00:18:57,908
(Everyone avoided using it.)

436
00:18:57,908 --> 00:18:58,938
- Not this.
- This is hard.

437
00:18:58,938 --> 00:19:00,538
It's hard to use it.

438
00:19:00,938 --> 00:19:04,078
I thought the bowl was really difficult to make use of.

439
00:19:04,238 --> 00:19:05,508
Seven sections?

440
00:19:05,848 --> 00:19:08,148
Can I utilize them all?

441
00:19:09,848 --> 00:19:13,548
The sales price is 11 dollars for every team.

442
00:19:13,848 --> 00:19:15,258
We don't have ingredients left.

443
00:19:15,258 --> 00:19:19,388
Also, eight additional ingredients are ready for you.

444
00:19:19,928 --> 00:19:21,458
They have more ingredients.

445
00:19:21,828 --> 00:19:24,498
Each person can choose...

446
00:19:24,498 --> 00:19:25,798
one ingredient.

447
00:19:26,228 --> 00:19:27,698
- Team leaders, - Open 1 by 1.

448
00:19:27,698 --> 00:19:29,438
- please choose your ingredient.
- This.

449
00:19:29,838 --> 00:19:32,408
- Ham, chicken.
- Shrimps. I'm sick of them.

450
00:19:32,738 --> 00:19:35,078
Eggs, ham, and beef loin.

451
00:19:35,638 --> 00:19:36,908
Boneless drumsticks.

452
00:19:36,908 --> 00:19:38,848
Fried chicken in hot and sour soy sauce or spicy garlic fried chicken?

453
00:19:38,848 --> 00:19:40,478
We still have shrimps left.

454
00:19:40,478 --> 00:19:41,478
Yes.

455
00:19:41,678 --> 00:19:43,818
I haven't thought of the menu yet.

456
00:19:44,048 --> 00:19:47,288
I chose the ingredient first and thought about it later.

457
00:19:47,648 --> 00:19:48,918
Shall we take potatoes?

458
00:19:48,918 --> 00:19:50,458
Because we have chicken.

459
00:19:50,458 --> 00:19:51,688
Take the potatoes.

460
00:19:52,558 --> 00:19:54,388
(Extra ingredients selection)

461
00:19:54,388 --> 00:19:55,428
(Lee Yeon Bok: Chicken, Kim Min Seong: Squid,)

462
00:19:55,428 --> 00:19:56,458
(Go Seok Hyun: Shrimp, Lee Sung Hoon: Eggs,)

463
00:19:56,458 --> 00:19:58,428
(Kim Ho Yoon: Canned ham, Kim Kwan Hoon: Beef loin)

464
00:19:58,428 --> 00:20:01,468
You have two hours to prepare.

465
00:20:02,538 --> 00:20:04,498
One hour before the business starts...

466
00:20:04,638 --> 00:20:05,638
Good luck.

467
00:20:05,638 --> 00:20:07,068
Only the team leaders will remain...

468
00:20:07,068 --> 00:20:08,238
- to prepare for the business.
- We can do it.

469
00:20:08,238 --> 00:20:09,308
Don't worry.

470
00:20:10,008 --> 00:20:11,878
The boss battle begins...

471
00:20:12,508 --> 00:20:14,308
at 6:30pm.

472
00:20:15,078 --> 00:20:19,018
You could become enemies who eliminate each other...

473
00:20:19,948 --> 00:20:23,158
or comrades who survive together.

474
00:20:24,258 --> 00:20:28,128
Please start preparing for business.

475
00:20:28,628 --> 00:20:29,828
Good luck.

476
00:20:29,828 --> 00:20:32,998
- Good luck.
- Good luck.

477
00:20:35,438 --> 00:20:37,638
How will two teams share?

478
00:20:38,838 --> 00:20:41,268
Chef, I'm sorry you're going through all this trouble because of us.

479
00:20:41,268 --> 00:20:42,978
- Why would you say that?
- I'm sorry.

480
00:20:43,108 --> 00:20:44,508
- As I said first, - Don't say that.

481
00:20:44,508 --> 00:20:45,948
I tried my best not to cause a nuisance.

482
00:20:45,948 --> 00:20:47,848
But it has come to this. I'm sorry.

483
00:20:47,848 --> 00:20:49,718
You never know what might happen.

484
00:20:49,948 --> 00:20:51,148
I'm sorry.

485
00:20:51,888 --> 00:20:53,248
I'll stir-fry it...

486
00:20:53,588 --> 00:20:55,458
I acted fine, but...

487
00:20:56,058 --> 00:20:59,788
We were leading in first place.

488
00:20:59,928 --> 00:21:02,828
In sixth place, Wandering Panda.

489
00:21:03,328 --> 00:21:04,998
- We're in last place.
- We're in last place.

490
00:21:06,028 --> 00:21:08,298
We experienced the two extremes.

491
00:21:09,168 --> 00:21:11,098
I'll survive no matter what.

492
00:21:11,198 --> 00:21:12,768
I won't just survive.

493
00:21:12,768 --> 00:21:14,938
I'll win first place.

494
00:21:15,038 --> 00:21:16,408
That's how I can save face.

495
00:21:16,808 --> 00:21:18,208
It's my pride.

496
00:21:21,178 --> 00:21:22,748
Can you pass me the bowl?

497
00:21:23,118 --> 00:21:24,788
The eight-section bowl?

498
00:21:26,448 --> 00:21:27,788
(Sucking his teeth)

499
00:21:28,518 --> 00:21:30,388
The bowl is the problem.

500
00:21:31,658 --> 00:21:33,828
When they'd announced the cauldron-shaped bowl,

501
00:21:33,828 --> 00:21:37,058
they said we didn't need to use the top part of the plate.

502
00:21:37,258 --> 00:21:39,368
When I think about it,

503
00:21:39,668 --> 00:21:42,868
most people won't use the top plate.

504
00:21:43,298 --> 00:21:45,508
"So I'll make use of this somehow."

505
00:21:45,708 --> 00:21:47,468
That was the first thought I had.

506
00:21:47,808 --> 00:21:51,278
You don't need to make multiple dishes for it.

507
00:21:51,708 --> 00:21:53,448
- But...
- You can cook some chicken...

508
00:21:53,448 --> 00:21:54,508
- But...
- and...

509
00:21:54,508 --> 00:21:56,518
the food in the middle is the bait.

510
00:21:56,648 --> 00:21:57,718
Sorry?

511
00:21:57,718 --> 00:21:59,018
It's better to use it.

512
00:21:59,548 --> 00:22:01,048
- Really?
- You can lure the customers.

513
00:22:01,418 --> 00:22:03,018
There are many empty spaces.

514
00:22:03,218 --> 00:22:05,788
I wanted to fill them up, just a bit for each at least.

515
00:22:06,128 --> 00:22:08,758
Not many chefs would be able to fill it up.

516
00:22:08,928 --> 00:22:10,698
I'll bring out the most of my skills.

517
00:22:11,498 --> 00:22:13,328
I'll fill up the eight sections.

518
00:22:13,928 --> 00:22:16,568
Two sections each.

519
00:22:17,538 --> 00:22:18,638
Two sections each.

520
00:22:18,638 --> 00:22:20,708
(4 more dishes to make)

521
00:22:20,708 --> 00:22:23,508
I'll make as many dishes as I can.

522
00:22:23,508 --> 00:22:24,578
(4 side dishes, 1 main dish)

523
00:22:24,578 --> 00:22:27,548
(He'll make 5 dishes in total.)

524
00:22:27,548 --> 00:22:29,248
The customers will look at the price and go,

525
00:22:29,248 --> 00:22:31,918
"This food for this price?"

526
00:22:31,988 --> 00:22:33,388
That's my strategy.

527
00:22:33,388 --> 00:22:35,288
(His strategy is to be cost-effective.)

528
00:22:35,288 --> 00:22:36,558
The ingredients are the problem.

529
